  slide "placement-decision" {
    eyebrow: "Decisions · 15 of 16"
    title: "Placement decides topology and shipping"
    lede: "Same-host routes can concatenate local files directly, and a same-host aggregator tree is always honored without any wiring requirement. Cross-host placement adds Stage G input reconstruction and Stage E artifact upload around the same execution route: an externally placed tree intent falls back flat without operator DNS wiring, so cells never ship into a void."
    narration: "Placement adds topology and shipping decisions around the execution route. Cross-host runs reconstruct inputs through Stage G and upload artifacts through Stage E. A same-host aggregator tree is always honored, but an externally placed tree requires operator DNS wiring; without it, the controller falls back flat. Shipping changes byte placement, not measurement meaning."
    term: {
      word: "aggregation-topology decision"
      meaning: "Choose flat, local tree, or externally placed tree under deployment constraints."
    }
    points: [
      "Cross-host tree wiring is an admission decision, not best-effort discovery.",
      "Parquet emission depends on a parquet-bearing build and remains text-labeled.",
      "Shipping changes byte placement, not the measurement contract."
    ]
    caption: "deployment → topology + Stage E/G."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(id = "header", title = "DECISION · PLACEMENT + SHIPPING", caption = "deployment → topology + Stage E/G.")
